          "id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UPa_UPA00904",
          "lbl": "L-methionine biosynthesis via salvage pathway",
          "type": "CLASS",
          "meta": {
            "definition": {
              "val": "The methionine salvage pathway (MSP) is an important metabolic pathway in maintaining the amount of L-methionine as the amount of methionine in cells is typically limiting and its de novo biosynthesis is energetically expensive. Therefore, L-methionine is salvaged from S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine (MTA), the end-product of spermidine biosynthesis.",
